132. POWER OF TWO USING BITWISE OPERATOR
============================================================

For a positive integer n:

    n is a power of two if:

    (n & (n - 1)) == 0


Example:

    n = 8

Binary:

    1000

n - 1:

    0111

AND:

    1000
    0111
    ----
    0000


Therefore 8 is a power of two.


But remember to ensure:

    n > 0


Example:

    int is_power_of_two(unsigned int n)
    {
        return n != 0 && (n & (n - 1)) == 0;
    }


