133. SWAPPING USING XOR — INTERVIEW CONCEPT
============================================================

You may see:

    a ^= b;
    b ^= a;
    a ^= b;


This can swap two integers under appropriate conditions.

However, it is generally NOT recommended in production code.

Prefer:

    int temp = a;
    a = b;
    b = temp;


Why?

    - clearer
    - easier to maintain
    - fewer edge cases
    - easier for other programmers to understand


Know XOR swap for interviews, but prefer readable code.


