134. BIT COUNTING CONCEPT
============================================================

A classic technique:

    while (x != 0)
    {
        x &= (x - 1);
        count++;
    }


Each iteration removes the lowest set bit.


Example:

    x = 13

Binary:

    1101


Repeated operation:

    1101
    1100
    1000
    0000


Number of iterations:

    3


Therefore:

    popcount(13) = 3


