============================================================
136. SIGNED/UNSIGNED COMPARISON WARNING
============================================================

Be careful when comparing signed and unsigned integers.

Example:

    int a = -1;
    unsigned int b = 1;

    if (a < b)
    {
        ...
    }


The result may surprise beginners because usual arithmetic
conversions can convert the signed value to unsigned.


This is a major source of bugs in C.


For job-ready C, you should learn:

    integer promotions
    usual arithmetic conversions
    signed/unsigned conversion rules


in Chapter 6.


